From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Sun, 08 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Prevent vendor from overriding CPU ABI list properties

On Treble GSI devices the vendor build.prop is loaded after the system
build.prop. The GSI sets bare ro.product.cpu.abilist* to arm64-only
so that Vanadium (64-bit only, SDK 36) passes PackageManager's
forceMatch ABI check. Prevent vendor partitions from overriding these
properties, matching the existing protection for adb/secure/logd.
---
 init/property_service.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/init/property_service.cpp b/init/property_service.cpp
index 2ed1578..874accc 100644
--- a/init/property_service.cpp
+++ b/init/property_service.cpp
@@ -882,7 +882,7 @@ static void LoadProperties(char* data, const char* filter, const char* filename,
                                  << "' with new value '" << value << "'";
                     if(strcmp("ro.apex.updatable", key) == 0) {
                         LOG(WARNING) << "... Ignored apex by kernel version";
-                    } else if(strstr(key, "adb") || strstr(key, "secure") || strstr(key, "ro.logd.kernel")) {
+                    } else if(strstr(key, "adb") || strstr(key, "secure") || strstr(key, "ro.logd.kernel") || strcmp(key, "ro.product.cpu.abilist") == 0 || strcmp(key, "ro.product.cpu.abilist32") == 0 || strcmp(key, "ro.product.cpu.abilist64") == 0) {
                         LOG(WARNING) << "... Ignored";
                     } else {
                         it->second = new_value;
-- 
